## Ownership and borrowing

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `let b = a;` | Moves `a` (unless its type is `Copy`) |
| `f(&s)` / `f(&mut s)` | Lend it read-only / exclusively |
| `fn f(s: &str)`, `fn f(v: &[i32])` | Take slices: accepts `&String`, `&Vec`, arrays and literals |
| `s.clone()` | An independent copy |
| `fn longest<'a>(a: &'a str, b: &'a str) -> &'a str` | The result borrows from both arguments |
| Rule | Any number of `&` **or** exactly one `&mut`, never both at once |

