## Smart pointers and threads

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `Box::new(x)` | An owned value on the heap |
| `Rc::new(x)`, `Rc::clone(&a)` | Shared ownership, one thread |
| `RefCell::new(x)`, `.borrow()`, `.borrow_mut()` | Change through a shared reference, checked at run time |
| `thread::spawn(move \|\| ...)`, `handle.join().unwrap()` | Start a thread and wait for its result |
| `thread::scope(\|s\| { s.spawn(\|\| ...); })` | Threads that may borrow local data |
| `let (tx, rx) = mpsc::channel();` `tx.send(x)`, `for x in rx { }` | Message passing |
| `Arc::new(Mutex::new(x))`, `*m.lock().unwrap() += 1` | Shared changing state between threads |
| `AtomicU64::new(0)`, `fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed)` | Lock-free counters |

